# Declarative build config read by stuffbucket/macos-builder at build time.
# Every value here is untrusted client input to the builder: it is regex-validated
# and then gated against clients/stuffbucket/foodtruck.policy, which is owned by
# the builder and can only be changed via an approved build-config issue.
#
# `entitlements` must be one of the builder's ENUMERATED profiles
# (default | network | virtualization | bun-runtime) — a client can never supply
# an arbitrary entitlements path. FoodTruck needs no added capabilities, so
# `default` (hardened runtime only) is correct.
#
# `dmg_name` / `updater_name` let the client declare artifact filenames directly,
# so we get versioned names straight from the builder. {version} is the tag minus
# the leading "v". Without them the builder would emit "<volname>.dmg" /
# "<volname>.app.tar.gz" and we'd have to rename on the draft afterwards, the way
# maximal does.
#
# `updater` is requested for a specific reason: it is the ONLY artifact whose
# path staples the notarization ticket INTO the .app bundle. package-macos.sh
# gates `xcrun stapler staple "$APP"` on the updater being requested, so a
# dmg-only build ships an app that is notarized but carries no local ticket --
# Gatekeeper then has to verify online on first launch after the app is dragged
# out of the dmg. The updater tarball additionally carries a detached Ed25519
# (minisign) signature, giving two independent trust layers.

app_path     = dist/FoodTruck.app
volname      = FoodTruck
bundle_id    = co.stuffbucket.foodtruck
entitlements = default
artifact     = dmg,updater
dmg_name     = foodtruck-{version}-darwin-arm64.dmg
updater_name = foodtruck-{version}-darwin-arm64.app.tar.gz
